# CarveMe 1.2.2 with framed 0.5.1, metaGEM's version (its published GEMs say "built with CarveMe
# version 1.2.2"), verified 2026-09-22, digest
# sha256:af114f3be0e499fdce53c9d500502adc73804ae818b5e61b2d7624b783bd0076.
# Recipe: container_builds, carveme/ on feat/metagem.
#
# Python 3.12, because fir's only CPLEX (22.2) is built for 3.12 alone. That forces three changes
# from metaGEM's stack, all in the recipe, none to what a model contains:
# - patches/framed-0.5.1-py312-cplex22.patch changes container types only: collections.abc
#   imports, lists where CPLEX 22 rejects tuples and sets, and html.escape for the removed
#   cgi.escape. Without the last, framed drops every SBML note without failing.
# - bigg_proteins.dmnd is rebuilt from the bundled bigg_proteins.faa (84,674 sequences), since the
#   shipped 0.9-format database will not open in DIAMOND 2 and metaGEM pins diamond>=2.0.6.
#   That is carveme_init's own last step.
# - PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1, or a host ~/.local/lib/python3.12 shadows the image's packages.
#
# CAUTION `import carveme` selects CPLEX at import time and raises without it. Any step that
# imports carveme must put cplex_installation on PYTHONPATH.
#
# Verified on fir: metaGEM's carve call (-g M8 --mediadb metaGEM's media_db.tsv --fbc2) on
# iJO1366's proteins, with CPLEX 22.2: 2653 reactions, 1269 genes, gapfill added 3 reactions.
container: docker://quay.io/hallamlab/external_carveme:1.2.2
